EU finance ministers will discuss the  Commission's multi-billion euro  investment plan when they meet in  Brussels on the 27th of January  specifically they will discuss a recent  proposal by the Commission to establish  a European fund for strategic  investments the fund will finance large  numbers of projects to create jobs  enhance growth across the EU ministers  will learn more from the Commission on  how this new financial instrument will  remove barriers to investment and  leverage some 315 billion euros of  largely new money in the European Union  the new fund will be placed in the hands  of the European Investment Bank  ministers have welcomed the creation of  an advisory hub designed to assist  potential investors in making the most  out of the fund some Member States  question the new fund claiming it is  underfunded so ministers will try to  push for clarification the 28 ministers  are also expected to adopt a new measure  preventing corporate tax avoidance their  goal is to deter businesses from playing  with the blocks divergent tax laws
 

